// ⚠⚠ `npx tsc --noEmit` IN THIS DIRECTORY CHECKS **NOTHING** AND EXITS 0.
//
// This file is `files: []` plus project references — the standard Vite layout. That is
// what a solution-style root config IS, and it means the bare `tsc` command has no files
// to compile: it resolves this config, finds an empty file list, reports no errors and
// succeeds. Every "TS OK" ever taken from `tsc --noEmit` here was vacuous.
//
// ⚠ THE GATE IS `npm run check` (= `tsc -b --force`). Only `-b` follows the references
// below and actually compiles the two real projects. Do not "simplify" a check script
// back to `tsc --noEmit`.
//
// `--force` rather than plain `-b` because `-b` is incremental against the
// tsbuildinfo files: it is correct when timestamps are trustworthy, and a gate is
// exactly where you do not want to depend on that.
{
  "files": [],
  "references": [
    { "path": "./tsconfig.app.json" },
    { "path": "./tsconfig.node.json" }
  ]
}
